.TH "OSTRYA\-MEDIA" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-media \- Copy collection refs onto removable media, or pull them from it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya media [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy collection refs onto removable media, or pull them from it.
.PP
The media carry the commits of collection refs to a host with no network. The media repository is \fB\%MOUNT/.ostree/repo\fR on a mounted volume, in the layout that \fB\%ostree create\-usb\fR writes, so \fB\%ostree find\-remotes \-\-pull\fR reads it. \fB\%media import\fR also reads the media that \fB\%ostree create\-usb\fR writes. A nested subcommand is necessary. This command is an extension of ostrya.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "export"
Copy the commits of collection refs onto a mounted volume.
.PP
The command writes the media repository \fB\%MOUNT/.ostree/repo\fR\&. It does not check that MOUNT is a mount point. A new media repository is an archive repository. An existing media repository keeps its mode and its \fB\%collection\-id\fR\&. The command reads the ref files of this repository alone. It reads no \fB\%summary\fR and no ref under \fB\%refs/remotes/\fR\&. The tip commit of each ref must have an \fB\%ostree.collection\-binding\fR that states the collection id of the ref. If the commit has an \fB\%ostree.ref\-binding\fR, the binding must hold the name of the ref.
.PP
The command copies each commit at depth \%0, with its \fB\%\&.commitmeta\fR and the dependencies in field \%2, and copies no static delta. It writes the ref NAME of the collection ID to \fB\%refs/mirrors/ID/NAME\fR, or to \fB\%refs/heads/NAME\fR when ID is the \fB\%collection\-id\fR of the media repository. It moves a ref to an older commit with no error. Then it sets \fB\%[core] indexed\-deltas=true\fR, writes the summary of the media repository with no \fB\%ostree\-metadata\fR commit, and removes \fB\%summary.sig\fR\&.
.PP
Before the command creates a file on the volume, it checks and resolves each REF, and it reads the tip commit of each REF. It also checks the collection binding and the ref binding of each tip commit. It refuses a MOUNT whose \fB\%\&.ostree/repo\fR is this repository. If one of these checks fails, the command writes nothing on the volume. A failure after these checks can leave a repository with objects on the volume. Examples are a tip commit whose tree is not complete in this repository, and a full volume.
.PP
On success, the first line of standard output is the absolute path of the media repository. One line \fB\%@ID:NAME CHECKSUM\fR follows for each exported ref, in the order of the operands. On failure, the command writes one \fB\%error:\fR line to standard error and nothing to standard output, and exits \%1.
.PP
.nf
ostrya media export [OPTIONS] <MOUNT> <REF>...
.fi
.PP
Arguments:
.TP
\fIMOUNT\fR
The directory where the volume is mounted.
.TP
\fIREF...\fR
The refs to export.
.IP
NAME is the local ref \fB\%refs/heads/NAME\fR\&. It goes onto the media as \%@OWN:NAME, where OWN is the \fB\%collection\-id\fR of this repository, and a repository with no \fB\%collection\-id\fR refuses it. \%@ID:NAME is the ref NAME of the collection ID: \fB\%refs/heads/NAME\fR when ID is the \fB\%collection\-id\fR of this repository, and else \fB\%refs/mirrors/ID/NAME\fR\&. The command refuses \%REMOTE:NAME, and NAME with \%@OWN:NAME in one run. Without \%\-\-commit, a REF that occurs two times is exported one time.
.PP
Options:
.TP
\fB\-\-commit\fR \fICHECKSUM\fR
Export this commit as the one REF.
.IP
CHECKSUM is a full commit checksum in lower case. The repository must hold the commit, and the ref need not exist. The commit can be older than the commit of the ref on the media. The command refuses an abbreviated checksum, a ref name, and more than one REF.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-collection\fR \fIID\fR
Put each plain REF in the collection ID.
.IP
A plain NAME becomes \%@ID:NAME, and \%@ID:NAME stays. The command refuses \%@C:NAME with C other than ID.
.SS "import"
Pull collection refs from the media repository on a mounted volume.
.PP
Without \%\-\-mount, the command reads the mount table of the process and probes each mount. It skips a mount whose directory any user can write, such as \%/tmp or \%/dev/shm. On each mount, it probes each entry of \fB\%\&.ostree/repos.d/\fR, then \fB\%\&.ostree/repo\fR, \fB\%ostree/repo\fR, and \fB\%var/lib/flatpak/repo\fR\&. The media repository of a mount is the first of these repositories whose summary lists a collection ref. For the collection id that the summary states, the command does not count the anchor ref \fB\%ostree\-metadata\fR\&. The command skips a repository on another file system than the mount, a repository that it cannot read, and this repository. The command needs exactly one media repository.
.PP
A ref \%@ID:NAME is on the media when the ref files of the media repository and its summary both list it. For the collection id that the summary states, the command does not count the ref \fB\%ostree\-metadata\fR as listed, because it is the anchor ref of the media repository. The commit of the ref is the commit that the summary lists. The command reads no \fB\%summary.sig\fR\&. With no REF and no \%\-c, the command imports each ref on the media whose collection has a matched remote, and ignores each other collection.
.PP
The matched remote of the collection ID is the first remote, in the byte order of the names, whose \fB\%collection\-id\fR is ID. If no remote has that \fB\%collection\-id\fR, it is the first remote whose \fB\%mirrored\-collection\-ids\fR holds ID. The trust of the matched remote checks the commits of ID: \fB\%gpg\-verify\fR, \fB\%sign\-verify\fR, and their keys. If that trust checks no commit signature, the command checks the GPG signature of each commit with the keyring of the remote.
.PP
The command pulls each ref at depth \%0, with its own transaction, and reads no static delta. It writes the ref \%@ID:NAME to \fB\%refs/mirrors/ID/NAME\fR, or to \fB\%refs/heads/NAME\fR when ID is the \fB\%collection\-id\fR of this repository. The current ref is the ref at that place. A directory at that place, or a path to that place through a file, fails the read of the current ref. If this repository has no ref at that place, and the \fB\%collection\-id\fR of the matched remote R is ID, the current ref is \fB\%refs/remotes/R/NAME\fR\&. A remote ref whose commit this repository does not store is no current ref. Under the \fB\%collection\-id\fR of this repository, the command reads no ref under \fB\%refs/remotes/\fR\&. The command does not pull a ref whose current ref holds the commit of the media. It refuses a commit that is older than the commit of the current ref, a commit whose timestamp is not the timestamp that the summary lists for the ref, and a ref whose current ref it cannot read. If the command pulls a ref whose current ref is the ref at the place that the command writes, and this repository does not store the commit of the current ref, the command refuses the ref.
.PP
Before the first pull, the command checks each REF, finds the media repository, and finds each REF and the matched remote of each collection. If one of these checks fails, the command changes no ref, writes one \fB\%error:\fR line to standard error, and exits \%1. When it finds no media repository, one line \fB\%PATH: REASON\fR follows for each repository that it skipped.
.PP
Standard output has one line \fB\%@ID:NAME CHECKSUM\fR for each written ref, in the order of the import. A ref whose current ref holds the commit of the media prints no line. A refused ref does not stop the import. After the last pull, the command writes one line \fB\%error: @ID:NAME: TEXT\fR to standard error for each refused ref, then exits \%1.
.PP
.nf
ostrya media import [OPTIONS] [REF]...
.fi
.PP
Arguments:
.TP
\fIREF...\fR
The refs to import.
.IP
NAME is the ref \%@OWN:NAME, where OWN is the \fB\%collection\-id\fR of this repository, and a repository with no \fB\%collection\-id\fR refuses it. \%@ID:NAME is the ref NAME of the collection ID. \%@ID: is each ref of the collection ID on the media. The command refuses \%REMOTE:NAME, and NAME with \%@OWN:NAME in one run. A REF that occurs two times is imported one time.
.PP
Options:
.TP
\fB\-\-mount\fR \fIPATH\fR
Probe the directory PATH in place of the mount table.
.IP
PATH need not be a mount point. The command probes PATH also if any user can write it. The command probes the same paths under PATH, and the path of each repository must cross no mount point under PATH.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-collection\fR \fIID\fR
Put each plain REF in the collection ID.
.IP
A plain NAME becomes \%@ID:NAME, and \%@ID:NAME and \%@ID: stay. The command refuses \%@C:NAME and \%@C: with C other than ID. With no REF, the command imports each ref of ID on the media.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
